    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0736" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/32357: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d404-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-01T13:00:00+02:00">December 1, 1943—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1958. The following telegram has been sent to Cairo,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d404-f2"/> repeated for the Department’s information: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Most Immediate December 1, 1 p.m. Most secret for the President.</p>
                        <p>In a conversation with the Foreign Minister<anchor n="3" xml:id="d404-f3"
                            /> this morning he referred to your presence in Cairo and again
                            expressed the hope that a meeting could be arranged between Inonu and yourself.<anchor n="4"
                                xml:id="d404-f4"/> He intimated <pb facs="0737" n="633"
                                xml:id="pg633"/> that given sufficient notice Inonu could meet you in Aleppo, just
                            across the Turkish frontier.</p>
                        <p>For your information Aleppo is about 26 hours by special train from
                            Ankara and would seem satisfactory from a security point of view.</p>
                        <p>Please instruct the Security Officers to transmit any reply you may send
                            me as quickly as possible.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Steinhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d404-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d404-f1-content">
                <p>For earlier correspondence relating to arrangements for the Second Cairo
                    Conference, see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg43">pp.
                        43</ref>, <ref target="#pg386">386</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d404-f2" n="2" xml:id="d404-f2-content">
                <p>Not found in the Roosevelt Papers.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d404-f3" n="3" xml:id="d404-f3-content">
                <p>Numan Menemencioğlu.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d404-f4" n="4" xml:id="d404-f4-content">
                <p>For the previous expression of hope for such a meeting, see Steinhardt’s telegram 1869 of November 14,
                    1943, 5 p.m., <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg86">p.
                    86</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
